# What `docker build` may see. Both Dockerfiles build from the repository root (they need
# packages/shared too), so the whole repository is the "build context": everything not listed
# here is sent to Docker. Leaving things out keeps builds fast and keeps secrets out of images.

# Installed and built inside the image, never copied from the laptop (wrong OS, stale).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/web/next-env.d.ts
apps/api/data

# Secrets: production values come from the host's env file at run time (DESIGN.md §14.4).
.env
.env.*

# Not needed to build or run the apps.
.git
.github
.vscode
**/test
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/*.md
docs
docker-compose.yml
